WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.010
You wake up,

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:01.790
look in the mirror,

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.550
and there's a number above your head again.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:05.850
But this time,

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:06.790
it isn't money.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.350
Plus seventy-three.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.110
It's your karma.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.730
Every kind thing you've ever done,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.310
minus every cruel one,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.750
added into a single score.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:17.670
Everyone has one.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.610
For the next seven days,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.810
you can see exactly how good,

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:22.750
or how bad,

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.250
everyone really is.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.890
And by day seven,

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.050
the lowest number in the city will

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.070
belong to someone you'd never expect.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.630
At first, it's just fascinating.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.950
The barista who remembers everyone's

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.270
name is at plus four hundred and ten.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.230
The man yelling at his phone is at minus thirty-eight.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:40.610
Fair enough.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.870
But then you see the man in the expensive suit.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.550
The one who looks like he'd step

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.870
over you to catch a taxi.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.320
Plus two thousand,

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.530
three hundred.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.610
You don't know what he did.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:52.670
You'll never know.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.290
But he did a lot of it.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.350
And the little girl holding her mum's hand?

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.350
Plus ninety.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.450
Already beating you.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.410
Lesson one, before breakfast:

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:03.610
just like money,

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.950
you can't see goodness from the outside.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.030
Then you walk into work.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:09.430
And there's Kevin.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:12.670
Kevin, who forwards your emails and calls it teamwork.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.470
Kevin is at plus eight hundred and eighty.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.230
That's more than ten times your number.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.030
You can't stop staring,

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:20.930
so at lunch,

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:21.610
you ask around.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.050
Kevin covers night shifts for a

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.430
coworker whose kid is sick.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:26.710
Every week.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.410
He never mentioned it.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:30.350
You ask him why he never told anyone.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:31.630
He shrugs.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.560
"Didn't seem like the kind of thing you announce."

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.390
You've spent years deciding who Kevin was

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.110
from the tiny part of him you could see.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.450
You were wrong about his salary last week.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.150
You were wrong about this,

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:43.410
too.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.230
On day three,

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.550
a man at the mall hands you a free sample.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.570
He's smiling, but his number doesn't move.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:51.850
Not even by one.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.830
Because karma, you realize,

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:56.670
can tell the difference between a gift and a hook.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:58.210
And the hook works.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.650
In a famous experiment,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.450
a researcher bought people a can of Coke as a small,

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.410
unexpected favor.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.550
Later, he asked them to buy raffle tickets.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.290
The people who got the Coke bought

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.150
about twice as many tickets.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.190
Even the ones who didn't like him.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.950
A small favor makes us feel

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.370
like we owe something back.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.070
It's called reciprocity.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.510
It's one of the strongest forces in human behaviour,

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.430
and salespeople know it.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.050
Ever wondered why supermarkets hand out free samples?

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.530
Now you know.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.190
You buy the thing anyway.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:27.950
Your number drops by one,

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.890
for buying something you didn't need

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.710
with money you'd promised to save.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:33.750
So on day four,

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:34.910
you come up with a plan.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.910
You're going to farm karma.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.230
You help an old man carry his groceries.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.390
You hold doors.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.430
You tell everyone their haircut looks great.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.840
Your number goes up.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.590
Plus seventy-four.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:46.970
Plus seventy-five.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:47.430
Slowly.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:48.990
Painfully slowly.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.270
By evening, you've helped eleven people,

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:52.190
your feet hurt,

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.550
and you've gained four points.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.830
It's almost like the number knows

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.450
when kindness is a performance.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.530
Then, on the way home,

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:00.730
you buy two hot chocolates,

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.610
and for no reason at all,

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.250
you hand one to a stranger shivering at the bus stop.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.010
She looks at you like you just handed her the moon.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:09.310
Plus six.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:10.730
In one second.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.990
Psychologists actually tested this.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:14.410
They had people give hot chocolate

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.490
to strangers in a park,

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.670
then asked them to guess how the strangers would feel.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.470
The givers guessed wrong.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:20.530
Every time.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.150
The strangers felt much better

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.070
than the givers predicted.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.790
We constantly underestimate how much a

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:28.050
small kindness means to someone else.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:29.970
On day five,

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:30.830
you see her again.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.230
The woman from the bus stop.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.250
She's at the hospital entrance,

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.150
holding the door for a man on crutches.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:37.790
The man on crutches,

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.850
ten minutes later,

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.130
lets a mother with a crying

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.470
baby go ahead of him in line.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:42.570
And the mother,

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:43.530
on her way out,

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.830
pays for the coffee of the person behind her.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.170
One hot chocolate.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.650
Three more good things you

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.830
never would have known about.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.050
And none of them will ever know it started with you.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.330
Scientists have found something

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.390
like this in experiments.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.310
When people played games where

00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:59.550
they could share with a group,

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.950
generosity spread from person to person,

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.210
up to three steps away.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:06.210
Each extra bit of sharing ended up multiplied,

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.710
as others copied it.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.850
But here's the uncomfortable part.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.350
Selfishness spread just as easily.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.070
Every day, you're starting a chain reaction.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.850
You just never get to see where it ends.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.130
The only choice is which kind.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.250
Then, on day six,

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:22.090
something changes.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.530
Everyone can see everyone's karma.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.570
And the world goes a little crazy.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.210
People start doing good deeds for the camera.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.530
Restaurants only let in high numbers.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.510
Dating apps sort by karma.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.650
Within hours, someone builds an app

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.250
that ranks everyone in the city,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.010
live.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.110
That evening, Leo calls you.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.530
His number dropped after he snapped at a waiter,

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.290
and now strangers are staring at him.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.350
He sounds scared.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.510
"What if people only ever see the worst thing I did?"

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.510
And people with low numbers

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:51.490
get treated like criminals.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.550
Then something strange happens.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.950
A man in your building loses his job.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.130
And the neighbours whisper,

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.770
"He must have deserved it."

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.290
But you can see his number.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:01.777
Plus one thousand,

00:05:01.777 --> 00:05:03.390
nine hundred and fifty.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.670
Psychologists call this the just-world belief.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.850
We want to believe the world is fair,

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.550
that good things happen to good people

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.170
and bad things happen to bad ones.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.490
So when something bad happens to someone,

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.850
we quietly assume they earned it.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.450
It makes us feel safe.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.190
And it makes us cruel.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.170
Sometimes, bad things happen to

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.110
people with great numbers.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.110
Remember the lowest number in the city?

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:27.330
The one you were never supposed to expect?

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.810
On day seven,

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.130
you finally find it.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.670
It's above a woman in a grey uniform,

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.490
standing next to a parking meter.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.743
Minus four thousand,

00:05:36.743 --> 00:05:38.850
one hundred and twenty.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.070
She's a parking officer.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.110
Every day, people curse at her,

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:43.230
slam their car doors,

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.210
and wish her the worst.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:45.910
But here's the thing.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.390
Her number isn't low because of what she's done.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.110
It's low because of what

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.830
everyone else has said to her.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.590
And when you look closer,

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:55.090
the number flickers.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.310
Underneath, faint and small,

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:58.890
there's a second one.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:00.800
Plus three thousand,

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.830
six hundred.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:02.650
Her real karma.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.390
The big red number was never hers.

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.850
It was ours.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:08.650
You walk over,

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:11.450
and you tell her she's doing a hard job well.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:12.710
She laughs.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.090
She says nobody has said that to her in eleven years.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.190
Then she tells you about a man who

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.350
once thanked her for a ticket,

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.330
because it reminded him to fix his brakes

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.970
before a long drive with his kids.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.850
She still remembers his face.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.790
At midnight, the numbers fade.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.730
The last one you see is your own.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.650
Plus eighty-one.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.390
Not huge.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:34.430
Not perfect.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:36.570
But higher than a week ago.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.850
And you realize what moved it

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.290
most wasn't the grand gestures.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:42.550
It was a hot chocolate.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:45.450
A text to Leo asking if he was okay.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:49.710
One kind sentence to a woman everyone else yells at.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.310
So before bed,

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.850
you send one more message.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:54.590
A thank-you to your mum,

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:56.750
for something she did fifteen years

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.290
ago that you never mentioned.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:00.550
Then Kevin texts you a photo.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.270
He's covering another night shift,

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.170
and the office coffee machine is broken again.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.510
You laugh, grab your coat,

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.690
and bring him a coffee.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.890
Some numbers you'll never see go up.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:14.330
Some kindness nobody will ever count.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:15.690
That's fine.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:16.950
It still counts.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.410
There's a famous study that found people

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.530
who spent money on others felt happier

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:24.250
than people who spent it on themselves.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.570
A later attempt to repeat it

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.830
didn't find the same effect,

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.170
so scientists are still arguing about it.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.650
But you don't need a study for this one.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:34.830
Here's what seven days of seeing

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.390
everyone's karma taught you.

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.910
You can't see goodness from the outside.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.870
Small kindness travels further than you think.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.670
Bad luck doesn't mean a bad person.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.770
And sometimes, the lowest number is

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.370
just the one everyone else wrote.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.890
Tomorrow, the numbers are gone.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.170
But you wake up hearing whispers.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.270
Everything everyone says about you,

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.550
when you're not in the room.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.350
If you want to hear it too,

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.110
subscribe.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.930
Because tomorrow, the whispers begin.
